# Rounded overlay surfaces

- Use explicit 8px corners for all current and new modal dialogs, sheets, drawers, size selectors, share dialogs, navigation overlays, and image viewers on mobile and desktop.
- Reuse `overlaySurfaceClass` from `src/lib/overlay-styles.ts` through the shared `DialogContent` and `SheetContent` components.
- Keep corners rounded at every breakpoint. Do not override with `rounded-none`, square bottom corners, or a different radius on overlay surfaces.
- Clip surface backgrounds, header/footer fills, and media to the rounded frame. Put overflowing content in an internal scrolling region; keep header and close controls reachable.
- Preserve full-viewport image viewing and safe-area insets. Rounding must not reduce image viewing space or change zoom/pan behavior.
- Keep focus indicators fully visible inside clipped surfaces and scroll areas. Preserve focus containment/return, Escape, browser Back, accessible names, and 44px close-button targets.
- Audit both the shared primitives and their callers when introducing or changing an overlay. Verify mobile and desktop, both themes, scrolling, and keyboard focus.
- This rule governs overlay surfaces. Preserve intentional circles/pills and square inner segments enclosed by an already-rounded control.
